.TH RASTERTOMFCJ5720DW 1 "November 2026" "MFC-J5720DW driver" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rastertomfcj5720dw \- convert CUPS Raster to Brother MFC-J5720DW printer data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rastertomfcj5720dw
.I job-id user title copies options
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B rastertomfcj5720dw
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read CUPS Raster from the named file or standard input and write the printer
stream to standard output. Diagnostics, page accounting and ink levels go to
standard error. The encoder is linked into the filter; no LPR command,
printconf program, shell wrapper, Ghostscript subprocess or RC file is used.
.PP
CUPS performs PDF/PostScript rendering, layout, page selection, software copies,
reverse ordering and odd-page duplex padding upstream. Pages are encoded in
the order received. The filter does not add another duplex blank page.
.PP
The initial implementation accepts uniform-size pages at 150 dpi for PlainFast
or 600 dpi for other quality settings, with chunked 8-bit RGB or white-based
grayscale. It checks the page dimensions and duplex settings against the PPD.
The inherited renderer consumes a complete RGB page for rotation and enhancement.
Small dimension differences from Brother's paper tables are cropped or padded
with white at the right and bottom edges, without rescaling.
.PP
Borderless sizes request paper-specific enlargement through the PPD's cupsReal0
field. The upstream renderer supplies a complete, unscaled page; this filter
uses bilinear interpolation to enlarge it. This avoids a Ghostscript 10.06
positioning defect with cupsBorderlessScalingFactor. Physical sheet dimensions
remain separate, and the encoder applies the corresponding image-edge placement.
Content near the edges can fall outside the sheet. An already-enlarged raster
using the standard CUPS factor is accepted without further enlargement.
All expanded pages in one job must have the same raster dimensions.
Existing queues must update their PPD to use local expansion.
The private cupsReal1 field specifies a downward placement correction in
millimeters. A4 uses a measured 1.5 mm adjustment within the overspray area;
other sizes use zero. This translation does not change the enlargement factor.
.PP
JPEG transfer modes use libjpeg-turbo through the libjpeg API. The filter
retains Brother framing and baseline YCbCr 4:2:2 compression parameters.
JPEG bytes and decoded pixels can differ slightly from the legacy compressor
because the library performs color conversion, chroma sampling and DCT.
.SH COLOR ENHANCEMENT
Enable BRColorEnhancement (Color Enhancement) to apply image adjustments.
BRColorDensity (Color Density) and BRWhiteBalance (White Balance) each accept
integer values from -2 through +2. Both default to zero, preserving the
existing enhancement settings. Zero is the default level, not an instruction
to disable automatic white-balance correction.
.PP
Color Density adjusts color intensity. White Balance adjusts the correction
derived from the image's light areas to reduce color casts in whites.
These are image adjustments, independent of printhead factory calibration
and cartridge ink levels. The two settings have no effect with enhancement
disabled or grayscale output selected. They apply before either raster or
JPEG encoding. Existing brightness, contrast and RGB controls are unchanged.
.PP
For example, add -o BRColorEnhancement=ON -o BRColorDensity=1
-o BRWhiteBalance=-1 to an lp command. Older queue PPDs without these options
continue using zero; update the queue's PPD to expose the new controls.
.SH FACTORY CALIBRATION
The BRCalibration PPD option, displayed as Printhead Calibration, controls
per-printer nozzle and density corrections.
Auto (Automatic) uses the queue's cached snapshot or retrieves one through
the CUPS backend. Refresh (Refresh Before Each Job) requests a new complete
snapshot before every job while selected and keeps the previous one on failure.
Off (Disabled) uses only the model profiles and does not access the calibration cache.
Auto is the default, including for queues with an older PPD.
.PP
Reading calibration changes no printer setting. Unsupported SNMP backends and
failed reads fall back to cached data or model defaults. Retrieval has an
eight-second budget in addition to ink polling. Corrections apply to supported
raster modes; host-side JPEG transfer bypasses their threshold calculations.
.PP
Cache identity uses the queue name and device URI, excluding credentials.
Select Refresh if another physical printer replaces one at the same address.
The snapshot is held for the entire job; partial reads are never installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PPD
Required path to the direct raster driver's PPD, normally supplied by CUPS.
.TP
.B DEVICE_URI
When present, request ink levels and factory calibration through the CUPS
backend's side channel. Unavailable readings do not prevent printing.
.TP
.B PRINTER
CUPS queue name, used with DEVICE_URI to identify its calibration cache.
.TP
.B CUPS_CACHEDIR
Directory for mfcj5720dw-*.calibration snapshots; default /var/cache/cups.
Files are created with mode 0600 and replaced atomically. An unwritable
directory still allows a fresh reading to be used for the current job.
.TP
.B MFCJ5720DW_PROFILE_DIR
Override the color-profile directory for isolated tests. The installation
default is /usr/share/mfcj5720dw/lut.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This is an experimental integration of the reconstructed encoder. Mixed page
sizes, raster formats other than those listed, and raster headers requesting
multiple copies are rejected. CUPS must expand copies before this filter.
The build still uses the shared encoder sources and verified non-executable
tables extracted from Brother's binary; color profiles remain Brother data.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means success, cancellation or help. One means a configuration, input or
rendering error. Two indicates an invalid invocation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mfcj5720dw_ink (1),
.BR commandtomfcj5720dw (1),
.BR cupsfilter (8),
.BR lp (1)
